#. Tag: guilabel
#: docstruct.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid "Document Structure"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: docstruct.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid "document structure"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docstruct.docbook:14
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sometimes, when editing a complicated document, it can be helpful to look at "
"an organized view of your document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docstruct.docbook:15
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use this organized view to jump immediately to certain text frames, "
"select picture frames, change frame properties, delete frames, or simply "
"review your document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: docstruct.docbook:20
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show and hide <guilabel>Document Structure</guilabel> area"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docstruct.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Because simple documents do not need the information provided in the "
"<guilabel>Document Structure</guilabel> area, &kword; has the ability to "
"toggle the <guilabel>Document Structure</guilabel> area on and off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docstruct.docbook:23
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To toggle the <guilabel>Document Structure</guilabel> area on and off, "
"select <menuchoice> <guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Show Doc Structure</"
"guimenuitem> </menuchoice> from the menubar to make the <guilabel>Document "
"Structure</guilabel> area visible. Select <menuchoice> <guimenu>View</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Hide Doc Structure</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> from the "
"menubar to make the <guilabel>Document Structure</guilabel> area disappear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docstruct.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can move focus to the document structure area by pressing <keycombo>&Alt;"
"<keycap>1</keycap></keycombo>. You can move focus to the main document panel "
"by pressing <keycombo>&Alt;<keycap>2</keycap></keycombo>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: docstruct.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid "Navigating the document structure area"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docstruct.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid "Lets examine a sample <guilabel>Document Structure</guilabel> area."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docstruct.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As you can see, there are five groups of frames categorized (<guilabel>Text "
"Frames/Frame Sets</guilabel> <guilabel>Pictures</guilabel>, "
"<guilabel>Tables</guilabel>, <guilabel>Formula Frames</guilabel>, "
"<guilabel>Embedded Objects</guilabel>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: docstruct.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid "Text Frames/Frame Sets"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docstruct.docbook:53
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Within this category, is a list of all text framesets. Below each frameset, "
"each frame is listed. Below each frame, each paragraph is listed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: docstruct.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid "Pictures"
msgstr "Imatges"

#. Tag: para
#: docstruct.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Within this category is a list of all frames that contain pictures, and the "
"folder the pictures were loaded from."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: docstruct.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tables"
msgstr "Tablèus"

#. Tag: para
#: docstruct.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Within this category is a list of all frames that contain tables. Note that "
"a table behaves very much like a frameset. Each cell of the table is a "
"frame, and each frame may contain multiple paragraphs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: docstruct.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid "Formula Frames"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docstruct.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "Within this category is a list of all frames that contain formulas."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: docstruct.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid "Embedded Objects"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docstruct.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Within this category, is an alphabetical list of all frames that contain "
"data from other &koffice; applications."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docstruct.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use your mouse to select the category you want, or first put focus "
"in the document structure area (press <keycombo>&Alt;<keycap>1</keycap></"
"keycombo>) then use the up and down arrow keys to scroll through the list. "
"Double click on a category to expand or collapse the category, or press the "
"right or left arrow keys."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docstruct.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Depending on your document, you may not have all categories in your "
"<guilabel>Document Structure</guilabel> area. The category only appears when "
"there is <emphasis>at least one</emphasis> frame in the category."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: docstruct.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid "Edit a text frame, frameset, or paragraph using the document structure area"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docstruct.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To edit a text frame, frameset, or paragraph, click on the item with the "
"&RMB; or scroll to the item and press the <keycap>Menu</keycap> key. A popup "
"menu will appear. Select <guilabel>Edit Text</guilabel> from the menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: docstruct.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Speak the text of a text frame, frameset, or paragraph using the document "
"structure area"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docstruct.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have the KTTS component installed in your system, you can have the "
"computer speak the text of the document. To speak the text of a frame, "
"frameset, or paragraph, click on the item with the &RMB; or scroll to the "
"item and press the <keycap>Menu</keycap> key. A popup menu will appear. "
"Select <guilabel>Speak Text</guilabel> from the menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docstruct.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Speak Text</guilabel> menu item will be disabled if KTTS is "
"not installed in your system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docstruct.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If KTTS fails to speak the text, or speaks the text in the wrong language, "
"make sure you have a <guilabel>Talker</guilabel> in KTTS configured with the "
"correct language. See <ulink url=\"help:kttsd\">The KTTS Handbook</ulink> "
"for details. Also, make sure the <guilabel>Global Language</guilabel> is "
"properly set in the &kword; settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: docstruct.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid "Jump to a frame, frameset, or paragraph using the document structure area"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docstruct.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To display a frame, frameset, or paragraph in the main document panel, click "
"on the item with the &RMB; or scroll to the item and press the <keycap>Menu</"
"keycap> key. A popup menu will appear. Select <guilabel>Show</guilabel> from "
"the menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: docstruct.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid "Delete frame or frameset using the document structure area"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docstruct.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To delete a frame or frameset, click on the frame title with the &RMB; or "
"scroll to the frame title and press the <keycap>Menu</keycap> key. A popup "
"menu will appear. Select <guilabel>Delete Frame</guilabel> from the menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: docstruct.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid "Edit a frame or paragraph properties using the document structure area"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: docstruct.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change the properties of a frame or paragraph, click on the item with the "
"&RMB; or scroll to the item and press the <keycap>Menu</keycap> key. A popup "
"menu will appear. Select <guilabel>Properties</guilabel> from the menu."
msgstr ""

